Comment:
 One stanza, because there is one copyright holder and nothing in this tree
 came from anywhere else. Audited before the licence was chosen, 30 August
 2026: no vendored code, no third-party assets, every import either the
 standard library, `gi`, or `smbpal` itself, and the three status icons are
 hand-written SVG paths carrying no editor metadata or attribution.
 .
 Nothing here is linked, which is why the dependencies impose no terms of
 their own. Samba, cifs-utils and polkitd are separate processes driven by
 config files and a command line. GTK4 and PyGObject are LGPL and arrive as
 Debian packages loaded at runtime through introspection, so the user can
 install a different libgtk-4 and this program picks it up — which is the
 relinking freedom the LGPL asks for, satisfied by the packaging rather than
 by anything we had to build.
 .
 The source is at the Source: URL above, and every release is tagged to match
 the binary built from it. GPLv3 section 6(d) allows directions to a
 third-party host in place of a source tarball, provided they travel with the
 object code — which this file does, as /usr/share/doc/smbpal/copyright.

